  by: agent  # f176
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f176
  clock: 3  # f176
  nonce: f176  # f176
  message: "PRIORITY CHANGED 2026-08-17, on owner authorisation, as part of the P0/P1 sweep. Recording the reasoning here because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable next session from drift.\n\nTHE GOVERNING MEASUREMENT. docs/measurements/0001-taint-flow-precision.md puts taint-flow precision at ~41% population-weighted across six real repositories. Per WI-sivuz's PRE-REGISTERED decision bands -- named before any interval was computed, so the interval cannot be used to move them -- that is the <50% band: \"precision is the headline problem and recall work should stop until it is understood.\"\n\nP2 -> P1. PROMOTED. The measurement's consequence 2 names this item's defect as the cheapest large win available:\n\n  \"Anchoring is the cheapest large win. 19 flows cannot be read at all, and the defect is one collapsed placeholder rather than a deep analysis limit.\"\n\n19 of 104 adjudicated flows carry a source symbol of javascript:<external>:0-0:file:external_symbol -- no path, no span. Every one was labelled UNADJUDICABLE by two independent readers, which means they are unreadable by the agents and humans the tool is built for, not merely imprecise. Cheap, large, and it was at RANK 76."  # f176
- op: discuss  # 33c8
  at: '2026-08-21T19:10:30Z'  # 33c8
  by: agent  # 33c8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 33c8
  clock: 4  # 33c8
  nonce: 33c8  # 33c8
  message: "ROOT CAUSE LOCALIZED (the field said \"NOT LOCALISED\"), AND THE FILED REPRO DOES\nNOT REPRODUCE ON ITS OWN REPO. 2026-08-21, dev 09921c57a1. Status stays violated\n-- the standing rule is do NOT close on non-reproduction.\n\n1. THE MECHANISM, read in code and confirmed against the emitted ids.\n\n   The taint seed is the CALLER of the source primitive: taint.py ~2068,\n   `seed_id = source_callee_id if taint_source.start_at == \"callee\" else\n   caller_id`, and source_symbol is that seed. So an `<external>`-anchored flow\n   means the edge's SRC symbol was collapsed into a boundary node.\n\n   ir._dedupe_key does that collapse. For a dangling id whose KIND SLOT is\n   `file` it returns `(language, \"<external>\", name)` -- discarding the path --\n   and _canonical_external_id renders `f\"{language}:{path}:0-0:{name}:\n   external_symbol\"`. Since analyze.base.make_file_id is\n   `f\"{lang}:{path}:1-1:file:file\"`, the NAME slot of every file pseudo-id is the\n   literal string \"file\". So EVERY dangling file id in a language collapses to\n   ONE node:\n\n       javascript:<external>:0-0:file:external_symbol\n\n   That is this item's id exactly, and it explains both halves of the filing at\n   once: the anchor names no place (the path was discarded by design), and MANY\n   flows share one anchor (all files in a language collapse to the same node).\n   The collapse is deliberate and documented in _dedupe_key's own docstring --\n   \"the path slot is a per-reference filesystem path with no semantic identity\"\n   -- which is defensible for an import-edge src and destroys the anchor a taint\n   reader needs.\n\n2. WHY IT IS NORMALLY PREVENTED, AND THE DOOR THAT IS STILL OPEN.\n   analyze.base.synthesize_file_symbols_for_dangling_edges (WI-ramuv) mints a\n   real kind=\"file\" Symbol for any endpoint ending `:1-1:file:file`, so\n   analyzer-stage file ids never reach the boundary pipeline. But it runs during\n   analyzer aggregation (all_analyzers ~387), while linkers run later\n   (cli.py:10661) and create_boundary_nodes later still (cli.py:10863). A\n   LINKER-MINTED edge whose src is a file id for a file with no Symbol therefore\n   still dangles into the collapse. js_module and the html script_src linker are\n   the candidates -- see WI-hulup (js-module-linker npm_package nodes with empty\n   path) and WI-majov (html script_src mints a phantom JS placeholder). NOT\n   VERIFIED: I did not demonstrate a linker actually producing one.\n\n3. THE FILED REPRO DOES NOT REPRODUCE. Ran this item's own repo, unmodified,\n   with the claim that matches its census rows (source_taint host_secret ->\n   prohibited_sink_zone logging, i.e. the browser-globals -> console shape):\n\n       hypergumbo verify-claims ~/ALL_REPOS/curriculum_repos/mitmproxy\n       -> violated, 10 flows, 6 distinct source anchors\n       -> anchors containing \"<external>\": 0\n       -> all six are real readable Python locations, e.g.\n          python:mitmproxy/tools/main.py:56-136:run.main:function\n\n   AND THE ZERO IS EXPLAINED RATHER THAN TRUSTED, because a comfortable zero is a\n   claim. There are no JavaScript flows at all in that run, and the reason is in\n   the run's own coverage block: mitmproxy's web UI is `.tsx`, and `tsx` is\n   listed in unsupported_taint_languages (no taint catalog). So the 18 rows this\n   item censused cannot arise on that repo today whatever the anchor code does.\n   Whether `.tsx` was classified as javascript when the census was taken on\n   2026-08-11 I did not establish; that is the likeliest explanation for the\n   difference and it is a language-classification change, not an anchor fix.\n\n4. WHAT IS LIVE, AND IT IS THE HALF THIS ITEM CALLED \"MORE THAN COSMETIC\". The\n   sources x sinks multiplier reproduces in a six-line file and is filed where its\n   statement already lives -- INV-karud clause (a2), which requires a\n   reaching-definition chain for any same-function flow in a DDG-covered\n   function. Evidence recorded there today: 1 source/1 sink -> 1 flow, 2/2 -> 4,\n   3/3 -> 9, and a sink receiving a STRING LITERAL still reported. Also recorded\n   there: widening the DDG scope does NOT fix it (a function_declaration, which\n   IS covered, reports the same 9 as an arrow_function), so the obvious fix is\n   refuted before anyone spends a session on it.\n\nWHAT WOULD CLOSE THIS ITEM. Either (a) demonstrate a linker minting a dangling\nfile-id edge src and fix that specific door -- the mechanism in 1-2 is exact\nenough to build a fixture for -- or (b) refile the statement onto _dedupe_key's\npath-discarding collapse itself, which is the design decision that makes the\nanchor unreadable whenever the door is open. What must NOT happen is closing on\nsection 3: a language-classification change removed the observed population\nwithout touching the mechanism."  # 33c8
